    "Description": "The mod_h2 Apache httpd module implements the HTTP2 protocol (h2+h2c) on top of libnghttp2 for httpd 2.4 servers.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* httpd: mod_proxy_http2: untrusted input from a client causes an assertion to fail in the Apache mod_proxy_http2 module (CVE-2025-49630)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
